nk function)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\)</span> (ordinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTree8TreeRank}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTree8TreeRank}_S\\)</span> (tree-rank predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"91f853557651cacc\" href=\"?note=91f853557651cacc\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-zfc-tree8-tree-rank.md\">../batch09/58-df-zfc-tree8-tree-rank.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZfcTree9WellFoundedRank}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{ZfcTree9WellFoundedRank}_S\\)</span> (rank-graph predicate defined here)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}tree9\\text{-}well\\text{-}founded\\text{-}rank}\\vdash\\mathrm{ZfcTree9WellFoundedRank}_S(\\alpha,s,T)\\leftrightarrow s\\in T\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\land\\exists\\rho\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTree8TreeRank}_S(\\rho,T)\\land\\alpha=\\rho(s)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}zfc\\text{-}tree9\\text{-}well\\text{-}founded\\text{-}rank}\\vdash\\mathrm{ZfcTree9WellFoundedRank}_S(\\alpha,s,T)\\leftrightarrow s\\in T\\land\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\land\\exists\\rho\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{ZfcTree8TreeRank}_S(\\rho,T)\\land\\alpha=\\rho(s)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The well-foundedness premise makes the recursive successor-rank supremum ordinal-valued.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":